    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that formula makes sense for the basics, but the lead times from shenzhen are pretty inconsistent. sometimes it takes 14 days, sometimes it's 45 because of shipping delays or factory holds. how should i adjust the safety stock math to account for that kind of high variability in the lead time itself? i dont want to end up with way too much capital tied up in inventory if the shipments arrive early, but i also cant afford to be empty-handed.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
