      "content": "When lead time variability is high, incorporating safety stock based on a quantitative service level (like 95%) is best. You'll need to calculate the standard deviation of both your demand *and* your lead time. The formula should then incorporate these standard deviations to determine the necessary buffer against uncertainty in both timing and quantity. This statistical approach ensures you have enough stock to cover extended delays without massively overstocking consistently.",
      "source": "target",
